@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+- A GPU-only image atlas page made since the last upload keeps its images when its texture is made: they were all in its pending regions, but the page was forgotten right after they were written, so each new page was placed and uploaded twice, a frame apart. Tests for the image budget, idle freeing and decode limits now assert the behaviour rather than the layer that refuses an oversized image.
